{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_axiom_3_chern","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L32-L52","doc":"**Axiom 3 — vanishing categorical Chern classes** (pattern C —\nnamed, not asserted).\n\n**Lemma statement** (from manuscript): under the proposition's\nhypothesis $c_{1}(\\mathrm{Ad}(P)) = c_{2}(\\mathrm{Ad}(P)) = 0$, the\ncategorical Chern classes\n$c_{i}(\\mathrm{Ad}(A)) := c_{i}(\\tau(\\mathrm{Ad}(A)))$ vanish,\nverifying axiom~(3) of\n[quantum observable universe](#def:quantum-observable-universe).\nFor $c_{2}(\\mathrm{Ad}(P)) \\neq 0$ the construction is replaced by\nthe modular tensor category $\\mathbf{Rep}_{k}(\\widehat{\\mathfrak{g}})$\nat level $k = \\langle c_{2}, [M] \\rangle$, with the level absorbed\ninto the ribbon twist.\n\nWe **name** the vanishing as a `Prop` over the context's primitive\nChern-class data, rather than projecting it from self-assuming\n`c_1_eq_zero`/`c_2_eq_zero` fields.  An instance of this proposition\nis the open vanishing claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:qou-exists-axiom-3","label":"lem:qou-exists-axiom-3","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-exists-axiom-3.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.c_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.c_2","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Second categorical Chern class `c_2(Ad(A))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.c_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.c_1","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L28-L28","doc":"First categorical Chern class `c_1(Ad(A))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.CategoricalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.CategoricalObj","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The categorical object / monoidal structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.ExistsAxiom3ChernContext","kind":"class","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/exists_axiom_3_chern.lean#L18-L30","doc":"Carrier for the `exists_axiom_3_chern` data — only the\nprimitive, non-conclusory fields (pattern C): the categorical\nobject and its first two categorical Chern classes\n`c_1, c_2 ∈ ℝ`.  The vanishing conclusion is **not** a field\nhere — it is the named proposition `exists_axiom_3_chern` below,\nso the claim is stated, not self-assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}